{{!-- A tab's view-state toggle: it writes nothing to the actor, so it is a <button> (a checkbox's
      change event would submit the whole form) and carries data-view-state, which keeps it live on
      a non-editable sheet. `flag` names the sheet-held flag it flips; `viewClass`, when given, is
      the class the sheet drops straight onto the live tab instead of re-rendering (see
      TabViewFlags). Callers pass already-localized `label`/`title` so the localization sweep still
      sees literal keys at the call site. --}}
<button type="button"
        class="stonetop-view-toggle{{#if active}} is-active{{/if}}"
        data-action="toggleTabView" data-view-flag="{{flag}}"{{#if viewClass}} data-view-class="{{viewClass}}"{{/if}}
        data-view-state title="{{title}}">
	<i class="fas {{icon}}"></i>
	<span>{{label}}</span>
</button>
